  "description": "A real Booking.com flight-booking-confirmation screenshot (JNB<->CPT round trip) came back with zero fields extracted. Two separate root causes, both fixed here: (1) the route was printed as \"Johannesburg (JNB) to Cape Town (CPT)\" - the two codes aren't adjacent to each other (a city name sits between them), so the direct \"CODE - CODE\"/\"CODE to CODE\" pattern couldn't see them; added a second route-matching path that looks for exactly two parenthesized 3-letter codes anywhere in the line. (2) JNB and CPT weren't in airportLookup.ts at all - the starter table was Philippines-centric and had no African airports; added South Africa's three major hubs. Also exercises the document-order date fallback fixed in the same change: neither leg is labeled \"departure\"/\"return\" here, so the fallback has to correctly treat the first-listed date (10 Apr, the JNB->CPT leg) as departure and the second (13 Apr, the CPT->JNB leg) as return, from real OCR text that also includes weekday names, mid-dots, and times on the same line as each date (e.g. \"Thu 10 Apr· 05:55 - Thu 10 Apr· 08:15\").",
